# Dear Prudence, verse (figure 131.2)
# Fourteen bars, AA'B plus a two-bar "washer". The upper row is the tenor voice walking down the
# semi-chromatic cliche D C B Bb A over the D pedal (the lower row). The first four bars are played
# twice ("2X"); "the crux" marks the B phrase, whose last bar moves off I to C and G under a
# "rapidly walking bass". Pollack types no tenor notes in the crux's third bar, where his
# "** rapidly walking bass ..." note begins; it is left silent here.
#? Tenor octave (D4 down to A3) chosen for range.
key D

system
voice "Tenor"   | [2X] D4 C4 | B3 Bb3 | A3 C4 | B3 Bb3 |
chords          | D{I} | - | - | - |

system the crux
voice "Tenor"   | A3 C4 | B3 Bb3 | r | r |
chords          | D | - | - | C{flat-VII} G{IV} |
caption ** rapidly walking bass ...

system
voice "Tenor"   | A3 C4 | B3 Bb3 |
chords          | D{I} | - |
